an easy choice for most to leave. We even had the privilege of briefly hosting lady [Lcea] Katta and her entourage recently. We did our best to make her comfortable.'\nYou say, 'their'\nVizra, magia mortis fortitio says, 'I was one of them, of course. When my people were approached many wanted to fight, as is our nature. The idea of joining with the `weak` Combine was inconceivable to most. I was something of an outcaste, which is what brought me to this far away location in the first place. So when the Combine arrived I took the opportunity to join. I believe I have proven my worth and skill. They have given me a unique title, and I hope to [teach] others once things are stabilized here in Kunark.'\nYou say, 'teach'\nVizra, magia mortis fortitio says, 'I have learned the art of necromancy from the greatest teachers in Neriak. I may not be the strongest practitioner of the art, but I understand the theory very well. It is my desire to teach anyone willing to learn. There is no reason that anyone should be kept from understanding what I know. Even the Koada`dal could learn the art, if only they could get over their prejudices.'\nYou say, 'Many'\nVizra, magia mortis fortitio says, 'I say many simply because some of my people did not return home. There were some that had been talking about how soft and friendly our people in Neriak had become. The steady stream of Teir'dal `heroes` that we have encountered in our work here has them worried. They believed that the heart of Hate was gone from their people. I fear that they may have done something foolish, for I saw them sneak off into the interior of Kunark rather than join the others that teleported home. Where they may have gone and why, I do not know.'\nYou say, 'Lcea'\nVizra, magia mortis fortitio says, 'Ah, well. I did happen to see her leaving in the night. I do tend to be a night owl by training, after all. They headed toward the Skyfire mountains. This did concern me, since the sarnak have a large presence there these days. I have even heard that some of those horrifying greenish sarnak were seen there recently. It is not my place to say, but I do worry for her safety. Her guards were, I understand, the best of the best. But those sarnak scared even my kinsmen. Are you here to [help] mistress Lcea?'\nYou say, 'help'\nVizra, magia mortis fortitio says, 'Ah, that is encouraging. There was a look in lady Katta's eyes that I have seen before. She seemed consumed with Hate, and I worry for her. I might recommend different approaches to Skyfire, depending on the size of force you can bring to bear. If you have a [large] force, I can send you right to the heart of the mountains. If you have a [smaller] contingent, perhaps a more circumspect entry would be best.'\nYou say, 'smaller'\nVizra, magia mortis fortitio says, 'Good, very good. Keep the lady safe. Let me know when you are [ready] and I can send you where you need to be.'\nYou have been assigned the task 'End of Empire'.\n\n---\n\nYou say, 'Hail, Lcea Katta'\nLcea Katta says, 'Well, it's the heroes. I'm glad to have you here, though disappointed that my father still hasn't seen [what needs to be done].'\nYou say, 'what needs to be done'\nLcea Katta says, 'I had hoped that my father would send Combine troops to help me deal with this issue. He needs to understand that we can't live here with these beasts. These hideous sarnak and their evil dragon masters will never let us live in peace. We need to stop them, I need to stop them, here and now. [Will] you help me? If not, it would be best for you to [leave] no before the fighting starts.'\nYou say, 'Will'\nLcea Katta says, 'That's good. I'm done waiting for my father's help. Prepare yourselves and let me know when you are ready to [start] this fight. I suspect that once we charge that hill there will be no returning until the battle is won.'\nYou say, 'start'\n\n---\n\nThe event starts.\nLcea Katta says, 'Good. Let's put an end to this once and for all time.'\nKar`Zok Warleader Hegron shouts, 'Destroy these fools. Kunark is ours now!'\nTalendor shouts, 'If you wish to fight, then do so. Let us finally see if the Kar'Zok are as strong as they say. Until this is over, none of you leave!'\nTalendor will cast Talendor's Fiery Breath. On emote, this needs healed through.\nYou will begin with 3 Kar`zok mobs. Balance kill the mobs to not get overwhelemed.\nKar`zok Lifestealers will use Virulent Toxin, which will viral to group members.\nOnce you start getting Meteor emotes, you will need to click the shield looted from Kar`zok mobs in the center of the giant red circles to deflect meteors. It is best to do this during the later parts and just move out of the red circles before it due to click re-use time. Players in the red circle will be hit with Draconic Meteor, if not deflected.\nWhen Kar`Zok Warleader Hegron attacks, he will emote people about being doomed, they will be hit with Doomhammer, run away if you get the emote\nKar`Zok Warleader Hegron will also have a nearby emote that does Hammer Smash if you don't run out\nWhen Overking Bathezid is the final mob, simply range kill him to win.\nYou will want to loot Overking's Tooth [item=132221] during this mission to be used in the Veeshan's Peak key quest, Scaled Key [quest=9004].\n2. Kill Overking Bathezid. 0/1 Skyfire Mountians\n5. Open Chest. 0/1 Skyfire Mountains\n\n---\n\n**Achievements:**\nHero of The Skyfire Mountains [quest=8947]\nStalwart Guardian (Group) [quest=9013]\nNo Outbreaks (Group) [quest=9014]\nUnhammered (Group) [quest=9015]\n\n---\n\n**Reward(s):**\n212 platinum 5 gold\nYou gain Experince!\n125 Bathezid Trade Gems [item=131783]\n**Submitted by:** Gidono\n- Bathezid Trade Gem [item=131783]\n- Elegant Maul [item=131654]\n- Fire-Forged Embellished Hoop [item=131610]\n- Gatekeeper's Golden Ring [item=131630]\n- Llywelore's Earring of Tenacity [item=131608]\n- Overking's Tooth [item=132221]\n- Scale Touched Cap Facet [item=129014]\n- Scale Touched Gloves Facet [item=129035]\n- 