      },
      walkthrough = "Quest Started By: | Description:\n**Where:**\n- The Overthere [RoS]\n**Who:**\n- Krama Alaeus [ _Quests_]\nRating:\n0/0**_\\*__\\*__\\*__\\*__\\*_**\nInformation:\n**Level:** | 95\n**Maximum Level:** | 125\n**Monster Mission:** | No\n**Repeatable:** | Yes\n**Can Be Shrouded?:** | No\n**Quest Type:** | Quest\n**Quest Goal:**\n- Advancement\n- Experience\n- Loot\n- Money\n**Success Lockout Timer**: 01:00:00\n**Quest Items:**\n- Cliff Golem Heartstone [item=131516]\n**Related Zones:**\n- Howling Stones [RoS]\n**Related Creatures:**\n- Vizra, magia mortis fortitio [ _Raid and Mission_]\n- a crumbling cliff golem [npc=53297]\n- a rocky cliff golem [npc=53263]\n- a rubble golem [npc=53260]\n- a wayward cliff golem [npc=53271]\n- an arisen convert [npc=53544]\n**Related Quests:**\n- Partisan of The Overthere [quest=8921]\n- Testing the Waters [quest=8843]\n**Era:** | !Ring of Scale\nRecommended:\n**Group Size:** | Group\n**Min. # of Players:** | 1\n**Max. # of Players:** | 6\n**Appropriate Classes:**\n- All\n**Appropriate Races:**\n- All\nEntered: Thu Nov 2 00:24:23 2017\nModified: Fri Oct 4 01:37:10 2024 | | **Prerequisite Quests:** Testing the Waters [quest=8843].\nThis is a shared task.\nSeek out Krama Alaeus in The Overthere in the outpost just inside and to the left as your heading in. At /loc +1425, +1274, +1.\nYou say, 'Hail, Krama Alaeus'\nKrama Alaeus says, 'Ah, good to see you again, I wanted to thank you for your help with our [dire] issues with the wildlife here. I've only been here a short while, but things certainly seem to have changed a lot since I was [last here].'\nYou say, 'last here'\nKrama Alaeus says, 'It's been, what, fifteen years since I was last here. Back then this was a Tier`Dal outpost stuffed into the ruins of an old Iksar port. They never seemed to be interested in repairing or upgrading anything. Too busy sowing hatred, I suppose. But now things are very different. I have so many questions, and so few [answers].'\nYou say, 'answers'\nKrama Alaeus says, 'I would ask myself, but the folks here seem a bit put off by me. They asked me here to deal with the animals here, specifically in regards to their aggression. We solved the main issue, as you know. But these folks seem extremely disconnected from nature and vaguely distrustful of me. They just aren't open to my questions. But seeing that you are considered a hero among them, maybe you can [solve] some mysteries for me.'\nYou say, 'solve'\nKrama Alaeus says, 'Great! It's good to have a friend here. Thank you so much.'\nYou have been assigned the task 'For My Information'.\n\n---\n\n1\\. Talk to Combine locals about the Tier`dal. (The Overthere)\nSay \"tier dal\" to any regular, non-quest, dark elf NPC around, until you get an update.\n2\\. Talk to one of the Tier`dal that joined the Arisen. 0/1 (Howling Stones)\nThis is \"an arisen convert\" in Howling Stones, they spawn in the east wing, northeast area.\n3\\. Kill the Arisen that has attacked you. 0/1 (Howling Stones)\nKill an arisen convert. They are found in the furthest point of the east wing in the Howling Stones. They are not KOS, and they aren't social with the other mobs in the zone. They hit very hard -- as hard as nameds in the zone. Max hit of 46,500 was observed (non-tank), but fight seemed pretty standard otherwise.\n4\\. Tell Krama what you have learned 0/1 (The Overthere)\nGo back to the outpost in The Overthere and talk to Krama Alaeus.\nYou say, 'Hail, Krama Alaeus\nKrama Alaeus says 'It never fails to shock me how far these dark elves are willing to go for their hatred. Though I suppose cursing this place shouldn't surprise me, joining a cult to Venril Sathir seems very odd. If we're going to remain here, we should probably learn about those curses, right?\n5\\. Discover the nature of the curse on the dock, if you can. 0/1 (The Overthere)\nThis is located on the end of the old pirate ship near the dock at /loc +2844, +2159, -33.\nOnce you get there, you'll see the following yellow text.\nFor a brief moment you feel unbelievably cold. Light simply disappears around you. When you recover, you notice that much of the wood on you weapons and tools is fractured.\n6\\. See what you can learn about the curse placed on the cliff golems. 0/1 (ALL)\nFind Vizra, magia mortis fortitio in The Overthere outpost and say \"golem curse\" to her.\n7\\. Get heartstones from errant cliff 0/1 (The Overthere)\nFind a crumbling cliff golem, wayward cliff golem, a rocky cliff golem or a rubble golem and kill them until they drop a Cliff Golem Heartstone [item=131516].\n8\\. Give the stone to Vizra. 0/1 (The Overthere)\nGo back to the outpost and give Vizra, magia mortis fortitio the Cliff Golem Hearstone.\nVizra, magia mortis fortitio examines the wrinkled stone. 'Well, this certainly is interesting. Look carefully at this. It is starting to split into two pieces. And the magic on it is, well, best described as chaotic. This heart isn't like they used to be, for certain. I would say that the golem this came from was starting to split into two distinct units. I would also guess that this one would have a tendency to act independently, maybe even contrarily to its orders. It's pretty amazing, really. Shame to waste such power and creativity on such a useless thing.'\n9\\. Speak with Krama about the curses. 0/1 (The Overthere)\nHail Krama Alaeus.\nKrama Alaeus says, 'Horrible, really, that people could do such things. I wouldn't be surprised if those dark elves had a hand in the plague the sarnak created. I'm glad I'm not a member of this Combine thing. Would could really trust dark elves in your society? Well, thank you for your help. Good luck in the future.'\n\n---\n\nReward(s):\nExperience\n212 Platinum, 5 Gold\n**Submitted by:** Gidono",
    },
