      },
      walkthrough = "Quest Started By: | Description:\n**Where:**\n- The Overthere [RoS]\n**Who:**\n- Praetor Noctis Trayer [ _Quests_]\nRating:\n0/0**_\\*__\\*__\\*__\\*__\\*_**\nInformation:\n**Level:** | 95\n**Maximum Level:** | 125\n**Monster Mission:** | No\n**Repeatable:** | Yes\n**Can Be Shrouded?:** | No\n**Quest Type:** | Quest\n**Quest Goal:**\n- Advancement\n- Experience\n- Loot\n- Money\n**Related Zones:**\n- Howling Stones [RoS]\n**Related Creatures:**\n- Deralin, dread Arisen [npc=53819]\n**Related Quests:**\n- For My Information [quest=8852]\n- Partisan of The Howling Stones [quest=8926]\n- Testing the Waters [quest=8843]\n- The Arisen [quest=8910]\n- The Dragons' Graveyard [quest=8849]\n- The Orb of Fire [quest=8898]\n- The Orb of Luclin [quest=8893]\n- Trail of Discovery [quest=8911]\n- What Makes a Scorpiki? [quest=8853]\n**Era:** | !Ring of Scale\nRecommended:\n**Group Size:** | Solo\n**Min. # of Players:** | 1\n**Max. # of Players:** | 6\n**Appropriate Classes:**\n- All\n**Appropriate Races:**\n- All\nEntered: Fri Dec 1 22:20:33 2017\nModified: Tue Dec 5 05:21:04 2023 | | **Prerequisite Quests:** Testing the Waters [quest=8843], For My Information [quest=8852], What Makes a Scorpiki? [quest=8853], The Dragons' Graveyard, The Orb of Luclin [quest=8849], The Orb of Fire [quest=8898], The Arisen [quest=8910], Trial of Discovery [quest=8911].\nTalk to Praetor Noctis Trayer in The Overthere outpost.\nRequest Phrase: help\n\n---\n\n1\\. Meet Drusella. She will answer Rile's call where she usually resides. 0/1 (Howling Stones)\nThe room must be cleared before she will appear.\nGhost of Rile Sathir says, 'Mother, come out. I must speak with you.'\nDrusella Sathir says, 'Rile. I have remained hidden, at your request. And now you call for me with these creatures present? Did you call me here to destroy them? I shall do so.'\nGhost of Rile Sathir says, 'No, mother, no. These are here to help us. No, don't bother telling me how we cannot trust the soft skins. I have chosen carefully. We must solve this problem, and these people can help.'\nDrusella Sathir says, 'I don't trust them. And I don't... They come! I can feel their presence!'\nGhost of Rile Sathir says, 'Now is when you can prove yourselves. Stop these Arisen.'\n2\\. Defeat the Arisen that have come to take Drusella. 0/1 (Howling Stones)\nDefeat three waves of 2 Arisen mobs, last wave being Deralin the dread Arisen alone.\n3\\. Stop Venril from taking Drusella. 0/1 (Howling Stones)\nYou must be in the east wing in the northern most room where Drusella is to get achievement.\nI set up at the far end where the map shows a gate to Overthere. this hallway at the end corner is a safe spot. I cleared the room and watched the dialog.\nRoom will repop as you pull the arisen mobs that spawn and path to Drusella. I pulled and kill in previously mentioned corner.\nDeralin is not quite as tough as the Named mobs for the zone but he is close.\nOnce he is dead you need someone in the room with Drusella for the update.\nVenril Sathir says, 'They do not come, darling, I do. And you, son, I thought you gone forever. I am glad that you have come.'\nGhost of Rile Sathir says, 'That must be a joke, father. You stole my life, do not pretend to be pleased that I am not gone entirely. Now you seek to destroy what remains of my mother too? I will not allow it!'\nVenril Sathir says, 'Destroy her? Never! She is everything in the world to me. Worth more than anyone, anything. Even more than the Empire I created.'\nDrusella Sathir says, 'Still? You still care for me?'\nVenril Sathir says, 'Of course! I have come to restore your life. All you must do is trust me. Come away with me and I will prove my love.'\nGhost of Rile Sathir says, 'No! He lies! He always lies! Don't trust him. Mother! He is wearing my body! How can you trust him ever again?'\nDrusella Sathir says, 'I'm sorry son. We all make rash decisions. I cannot turn away from him now. Once I am restored we shall return and restore you as well. Believe me son, you will live again too.'\nVenril Sathir says, 'Goodbye, son.'\nGhost of Rile Sathir hangs his ghostly head. 'I don't like this, not one bit. He can't be planning to help her. Helping others is never on his mind. Please, gather your allies. Find a way to stop him.' The sad ghost fades away.\n\n---\n\nAchievements\nPartisan of The Howling Stones [quest=8926]\n\n---\n\nReward(s):\nExperience\n318 Platinum, 7 Gold, 5 Silver\n**Submitted by:** Gidono",
